  "literature_notes": "L2 (PMC6724686) describes an HA tag in the P2-M4 interdomain of hK2P17.1 (TALK-2/TASK-4), a close K2P ortholog, using the same Friedreich et al. method as L1. Because L2 names no residue number for KCNK5 itself, it cannot pin an independent junction and does not add a second site; it corroborates the P2-M4 loop as a permissive region but is fully subsumed by L1. The first extracellular region (residues 27\u2013112, between TM1 and TM2) contains a cysteine at position 51 that likely participates in a conserved K2P disulfide; no ledger line reports a tag insertion there, so no site is proposed for that loop. The large intracellular C-terminal domain (residues 243\u2013499) is not an extracellular surface and is excluded. No ledger evidence supports any N-terminal or C-terminal extracellular tag for KCNK5.",
